Read CONTRACT.md, then core/contract.ts. To add a variant, export a value of your slot's type and append it to your folder's index.ts registry (the first entry is the default): World settings shows it as a card in its slot's strip, `?<slot>=<id>` selects it, the layout reflows the line from its `footprint`, and the camera's station stop frames its `frame` points. Draw in your station frame (the world shifted by the layout); the board and integrator draw in the board-local frame. Colors come from `Tokens` only. Read sim events with `useSimEvents(sim, fn)` and world anchors with core/line.ts helpers, never another station's constants; code that runs after the frame it was created in reads `sim.wanted`, never a captured `lab`. Verify with `bun check`, `bun run test` and `bun run compiler:report` from app/. Budget: < 150 draw calls real, < 250 viral.
